// Kamerton app (naryad Н1-06): the Telegram long-polling cycle in ONE
// serve program — deploy contract of kamerton.service
// (ExecStart: mlog serve /data/kamerton/app.mlog). The naryad fixes the
// shape: "два cron-тика в одном .mlog" — the morning tick proposes an
// arm (consumes the Н1-05 bandit core mirrored below) and asks for a
// prediction, the evening tick drains getUpdates, writes the answers
// into trial/response and closes unanswered trials as misses at 02:00
// local.
//
// ── Design decisions fixed here (in-boundary choices; the naryad fixes
//    the requirements, not the parametrisation) ─────────────────────────
//   1. Registration: the serve process runs NO top-level statements and
//     NO on_session_start hook at boot (the serve probe: hook file
//     absent, jobs=0). Cron jobs are registered IDEMPOTENTLY from the
//     /setup route (cron_list guard -> cron_add only when missing) and
//     carried across restarts by `memory { persist }` — the jobs and
//     the getUpdates offset survive the service restart (the
//     acceptance row; verified by the serve probes in the worklog).
//   2. Timezone: cron_add matches windows in the job's tz (default
//     MLOG_CRON_TZ else UTC), the deploy allowlist opens
//     KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET (hours, float; MSK=3). The tick expressions
//     are computed FROM the offset with the local wall-clock minutes
//     folded to UTC (no modulo operator — to_int truncation, the
//     bandit explore-idx precedent): 07:00 local under MSK registers
//     as "0 4 * * *", 02:00 local as "0 23 * * *".
//   3. Chat protocol (minimal, wave 1): the morning message proposes
//     the arm and asks for a prediction; the owner answers "p:<0..1>"
//     (prediction depth), "m:<0..1>" (the moment response), anything
//     else is appended to trial.free_note. Every outgoing text passes
//     escape_html — the DB output never reaches the chat raw.
//   4. Exactly-once posture: the Telegram offset (kv tg_offset) is
//     advanced AFTER a batch is processed; a crash before the advance
//     replays the batch and the DB guards make the replay idempotent —
//     the moment insert is guarded by (trial_id, kind), the prediction
//     UPDATE fills an untouched default only, misses are status flips.
//     A repeated free-note append is the one accepted dup window and
//     is declared loudly here.
//   5. Network posture: every http_get carries the per-call deadline
//     (№592) inside 1..=300; the outcome taxonomy is consumed through
//     the sanitize-then-decide form — escape_html (Sanitized =
//     public/trusted) decides the control flow, never the raw label.
//     send_message reads TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN from the process env
//     itself and degrades to the [AUDIT] stub without it (probe-pinned),
//     so tests never touch the network.
//   6. Trust boundaries: fetch_updates returns UNTRUSTED network data;
//     the whole update-processing chain runs inside ONE annotated
//     boundary pattern (the parity-tick-route fire_job precedent) —
//     inside it the data is sanctioned and the DB guards decide;
//     outside it the return is never echoed or branched on. The chat
//     filter compares SANITIZED projections.
//   7. Composition: no cross-file imports exist in the language, so
//     this file carries byte-identical mirrors of the store schema
//     (the bandit.mlog precedent), the bandit decision core and the
//     telegram pure core. The canonical copies live in
//     src/bandit/bandit.mlog and src/telegram/telegram.mlog; the
//     mirror modules carry the APP-MIRROR markers and the block
//     equality is verified by the verifier script recorded in the
//     naryad worklog (read_file refuses *.mlog paths — the
//     №455-sensitive list — so the pin lives outside the language).
//
// Language-discipline notes (§2, declared loudly where relevant):
//   - RESPOND_SWALLOWED (v0.28.2, security Y-1): every respond() is
//     written `return respond(...)` — the fail-closed startup refusal
//     of bare tail responds is the contract on both backends.
//   - env() in route bodies and cron-tick bodies is gated by №259;
//     every name read here (KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN, KAMERTON_CHAT_ID,
//     KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET) is opened by deploy/env.allowlist through
//     METALOGOS_ENV_ALLOWLIST (install.sh derives the runtime value).
//     TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN is read INSIDE the send_message builtin
//     (process env) — deliberately NOT in the allowlist.
//   - The D2 loop defect (№598, unfixed in v0.28.2): every sink call
//     inside a loop body uses the assignment shape `let _ = f(...)`; a
//     bare call inside a mixed loop body corrupts the pattern return.
//   - NEW D2-family symptom isolated during this naryad (probe in the
//     worklog): a `while i < len(xs)` loop whose body can reach
//     cron_remove() MISCONVERGES — after the first removal the pass
//     silently drops the remaining iterations (and stdout prints after
//     the first remove are lost), so repeat runs diverge (0 or 2 jobs
//     instead of 1). Every cron-store pass here therefore runs as
//     `each` over the cron_list() snapshot; the symptom is declared to
//     the Metalogos- agent (v0.28.3 task file). The same family, third
//     case: a print() INSIDE an if-body that follows an effect call
//     (cron_remove) inside an each-body silently kills the SUBSEQUENT
//     if/add phase — the registration prints therefore happen ONCE as a
//     post-loop summary, never inside the loop bodies (probe: variant
//     A misconverges, variant B converges). Fourth case, cron-tick
//     lane: a bare `return` inside a nested if-body of a Unit tick
//     pattern dispatches as [UNDEFINED_VARIABLE] "undefined variable:
//     return" — the early-return guards therefore invert into
//     positive-branch blocks (no return under a nested if).
//   - No modulo operator (grammar v0.28.2); to_int truncation
//     arithmetic everywhere a remainder is needed.

// The deploy contract of Н1-02: KAMERTON_DB carries the plain database
// path; the VM lane resolves it lazily at the first db access (№758).
// This file carries NO test blocks: v0.28.2 has no single db-url form
// valid for both lanes (the interpreter test lane needs an entity-ref
// url for the schema replay; the serve boot pass refuses entity refs —
// the §2 declaration below), so the app's tests live in
// src/telegram/telegram.mlog against a literal in-memory db and the
// byte-identical mirror blocks; app.mlog stays the serve canon.
db { url: env("KAMERTON_DB") }

// The KV store carries the getUpdates offset AND the cron job store;
// without persist both die with the process (the serve probe logs).
memory { persist: "data/kamerton-kv.db" }

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: db-cycle (byte-identical to
//    src/telegram/telegram.mlog §db-cycle) ──────────────────────────────

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: db-cycle (byte-identical to
//    src/telegram/telegram.mlog §db-cycle) ──────────────────────────────

// ── The schema: the operator-mirror DDL path (§2 declaration) ─────────
// Затык §2 (v0.28.2, заявлен громко в PR/worklog): ONE db-url form for
// BOTH lanes does not exist — `mlog test` (interpreter) requires an
// entity-ref url for the schema replay at declaration time, while the
// serve boot pass refuses entity refs ([UNDEFINED_VARIABLE]) and only
// accepts inline env()/env_or()/literal (№758 lazy). The proposed and
// implemented exit: the schema-as-code block is replaced by the
// ADDITIVE-ONLY idempotent DDL literals of the operator mirror
// (migrations/0001_init.sql, ADR-0183) executed by ensure_schema() —
// called by both ticks and /setup before any query. Byte-equality of
// the DDL to the migration is pinned by the verifier script in the
// worklog.
pattern ensure_schema() -> Unit {
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS arm (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT, group_name TEXT, day_window TEXT, duration_min INTEGER DEFAULT '10', prior_mean REAL DEFAULT '0.0', prior_std REAL DEFAULT '1.0', active INTEGER DEFAULT '1', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS note (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, body TEXT, active INTEGER DEFAULT '1', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS trial (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, trial_date TEXT, day_window TEXT, arm_id INTEGER REFERENCES arm(id), note_id INTEGER REFERENCES note(id), status TEXT DEFAULT 'proposed', prediction_depth REAL DEFAULT '0.0', prediction_confidence REAL DEFAULT '0.0', moment_value REAL DEFAULT '0.0', moment_present INTEGER DEFAULT '0', moment_source TEXT DEFAULT '', next_day_value REAL DEFAULT '0.0', next_day_present INTEGER DEFAULT '0', action_value REAL DEFAULT '0.0', action_present INTEGER DEFAULT '0', reward REAL DEFAULT '0.0', free_note TEXT DEFAULT '', closed_at TEXT DEFAULT '', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS response (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, trial_id INTEGER REFERENCES trial(id), kind TEXT, depth REAL DEFAULT '0.0', details TEXT DEFAULT '', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS context (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, trial_id INTEGER REFERENCES trial(id), moon_phase TEXT DEFAULT '', weather TEXT DEFAULT '', sound_mode TEXT DEFAULT '', sleep_quality REAL DEFAULT '0.0', logged_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS candidate (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT, kind TEXT DEFAULT 'non_periodic', status TEXT DEFAULT 'candidate', stat_value REAL DEFAULT '0.0', threshold REAL DEFAULT '0.0', tested_at TEXT DEFAULT '', note TEXT DEFAULT '')", [])
  ensure_indexes()
}

pattern ensure_indexes() -> Unit {
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_trial_date ON trial(trial_date)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_trial_arm ON trial(arm_id)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_trial_status ON trial(status)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_response_trial ON response(trial_id)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_context_trial ON context(trial_id)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_candidate_name ON candidate(name)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_arm_active ON arm(active)")
}

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: store-core (the signatures mirror
//    src/store/store.mlog; equality pinned by the worklog script) ──────

pattern trial_by_id(trial_id: Float) -> List {
  return query("SELECT id, trial_date, day_window, arm_id, status, prediction_depth, prediction_confidence, moment_value, moment_present, moment_source, next_day_value, next_day_present, action_value, action_present, reward FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [trial_id])
}

pattern compute_reward(trial_id: Float) -> Float {
  let rows = query("SELECT moment_value, moment_present, next_day_value, next_day_present, action_value, action_present FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [trial_id])
  if len(rows) == 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  let r = rows[0]
  let mut acc = 0.0
  let mut wsum = 0.0
  if r.moment_present == 1.0 {
    acc = acc + 0.2 * r.moment_value
    wsum = wsum + 0.2
  }
  if r.next_day_present == 1.0 {
    acc = acc + 0.3 * r.next_day_value
    wsum = wsum + 0.3
  }
  if r.action_present == 1.0 {
    acc = acc + 0.5 * r.action_value
    wsum = wsum + 0.5
  }
  if wsum == 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  let reward = acc / wsum
  db_execute("UPDATE trial SET reward = ? WHERE id = ?", [reward, trial_id])
  return reward
}
// ── APP-MIRROR-END: store-core
pattern last_proposed_trial(local_date: String) -> List {
  return query("SELECT id, arm_id, day_window FROM trial WHERE status = 'proposed' AND trial_date = ? ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1", [local_date])
}

pattern close_stale_misses(local_date: String) -> Float {
  let stale = query("SELECT id FROM trial WHERE status = 'proposed' AND trial_date < ? AND arm_id IS NOT NULL", [local_date])
  let mut closed = 0.0
  each t in stale {
    let tid = t.id
    let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET status = 'missed', closed_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = ?", [tid])
    closed = closed + 1.0
  }
  return closed
}

pattern apply_answer(tid: Float, ans: Struct) -> String {
  if ans.kind == "prediction" {
    let rows = query("SELECT prediction_depth FROM trial WHERE id = ? AND status = 'proposed'", [tid])
    if len(rows) == 0.0 {
      return "no-open-trial"
    }
    if rows[0].prediction_depth != 0.0 {
      return "prediction-kept"
    }
    let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET prediction_depth = ? WHERE id = ?", [ans.value, tid])
    return "prediction"
  }
  if ans.kind == "moment" {
    let guard = query("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM response WHERE trial_id = ? AND kind = 'moment'", [tid])
    if guard[0].n > 0.0 {
      return "moment-kept"
    }
    let row = {trial_id: tid, kind: "moment", depth: ans.value, details: "telegram m:"}
    let _ = db_insert("response", row)
    let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET moment_value = ?, moment_present = 1, moment_source = 'subjective', status = 'completed' WHERE id = ?", [ans.value, tid])
    let _ = compute_reward(tid)
    return "moment"
  }
  let rows2 = query("SELECT free_note FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [tid])
  let mut note = ""
  if len(rows2) > 0.0 {
    note = rows2[0].free_note
  }
  let joined = note + " | " + escape_html(ans.text)
  let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET free_note = ? WHERE id = ?", [joined, tid])
  return "note"
}

pattern process_updates(updates: List<public, trusted>, chat_id: String<public, trusted>, local_date: String<public, trusted>, offset: Float) -> Unit {
  // The D2-family posture: the drain is a BARE each (db effects inside
  // the loop are the m0_row-proven shape), every diagnostic lives in
  // counters, ONE summary print after the loop. The chat filter
  // compares SANITIZED projections; the untrusted raw never branches.
  let mut processed = 0.0
  let mut predictions = 0.0
  let mut moments = 0.0
  let mut skipped = 0.0
  let mut last_id = 0 - 1.0
  each u in updates {
    last_id = json_get(u, "update_id", 0.0)
    let chat = to_string(json_get(u, "message.chat.id", 0.0))
    if escape_html(chat) == escape_html(chat_id) {
      let text = json_get(u, "message.text", "")
      if escape_html(text) != "" {
        let ans = parse_chat_text(text)
        let open = last_proposed_trial(local_date)
        if len(open) > 0.0 {
          let tid = open[0].id
          let applied = apply_answer(tid, ans)
          if applied == "prediction" {
            predictions = predictions + 1.0
            processed = processed + 1.0
          }
          if applied == "moment" {
            moments = moments + 1.0
            processed = processed + 1.0
          }
          if applied == "note" {
            processed = processed + 1.0
          }
          if applied == "no-open-trial" {
            skipped = skipped + 1.0
          }
        } else {
          skipped = skipped + 1.0
        }
      } else {
        skipped = skipped + 1.0
      }
    } else {
      skipped = skipped + 1.0
    }
  }
  // The offset advances AFTER the batch; a crash before the kv_set
  // replays the batch into the idempotent guards (design note 4).
  if last_id >= 0.0 {
    let next_offset = last_id + 1.0
    if next_offset != offset {
      let _ = kv_set("tg_offset", to_string(next_offset))
    }
  }
  let closed = close_stale_misses(local_date)
  let _ = send_message(chat_id, format_report(processed, closed, predictions, moments))
  print("[telegram] drain: processed=" + to_string(processed) + " closed=" + to_string(closed) + " predictions=" + to_string(predictions) + " moments=" + to_string(moments) + " skipped=" + to_string(skipped))
}

pattern has_job(expr: String, target: String) -> Bool {
  // each over the snapshot: the while+len shape misconverges when the
  // body can reach cron_remove (the worklog probe, the new D2-family
  // symptom) — this pass must stay removal-free AND each-shaped.
  let jobs = cron_list()
  let mut found = false
  each j in jobs {
    if j.cron_expr == expr and j.prompt == target {
      found = true
    }
  }
  return found
}

pattern setup_register() -> Unit {
  // The D2-family posture: NO prints and NO mixed statements inside the
  // loop bodies — the stale sweep runs as a bare each, the add phase
  // runs through precomputed flags, ONE summary print after everything
  // (the probe: variant A misconverges, variant B converges).
  let off = to_float(env_or("KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET", "0"))
  let morning = cron_expr_for(420.0, off)
  let evening = cron_expr_for(120.0, off)
  let jobs = cron_list()
  each j in jobs {
    if j.prompt == "tg_morning_tick" and j.cron_expr != morning {
      let _ = cron_remove(j.id)
    }
    if j.prompt == "tg_evening_tick" and j.cron_expr != evening {
      let _ = cron_remove(j.id)
    }
  }
  let add_m = has_job(morning, "tg_morning_tick") == false
  if add_m == true {
    let _ = cron_add(morning, "tg_morning_tick")
  }
  let add_e = has_job(evening, "tg_evening_tick") == false
  if add_e == true {
    let _ = cron_add(evening, "tg_evening_tick")
  }
  if add_m == true {
    print("[telegram] registered morning " + morning)
  }
  if add_e == true {
    print("[telegram] registered evening " + evening)
  }
}

// ── APP-MIRROR-END: db-cycle ─────────────────────────────────────────

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: bandit-core (the signatures mirror
//    src/bandit/bandit.mlog; equality pinned by the worklog script) ────
// Thompson Normal-Normal on the decayed rewards, the 20% forced
// exploration floor, the seed contract. The entity constants below are
// byte-identical to the bandit module's.

entity reward_obs_std: Float = 0.25
entity decay_tau_days: Float = 60.0
entity explore_every: Float = 5.0

pattern today_unix() -> Float {
  return date_parse_iso(date_format_iso(now_unix()))
}

pattern decay_weight(age_days: Float) -> Float {
  if age_days <= decay_tau_days {
    return 1.0
  }
  return exp((decay_tau_days - age_days) / decay_tau_days)
}

pattern arm_posterior(arm_id: Float, prior_mean: Float, prior_std: Float) -> List {
  let mut s0 = prior_std
  if s0 <= 0.0 {
    s0 = 1.0
  }
  let rows = query("SELECT reward, trial_date FROM trial WHERE arm_id = ? AND status = 'completed' AND (moment_present = 1 OR next_day_present = 1 OR action_present = 1)", [arm_id])
  let today = today_unix()
  let mut wsum = 0.0
  let mut xsum = 0.0
  each r in rows {
    let mut age = date_diff_days(today, date_parse_iso(r.trial_date))
    if age < 0.0 {
      age = 0.0
    }
    let w = decay_weight(age)
    wsum = wsum + w
    xsum = xsum + w * r.reward
  }
  let inv0 = 1.0 / (s0 * s0)
  let invr = 1.0 / (reward_obs_std * reward_obs_std)
  let precision = inv0 + wsum * invr
  let mean = (prior_mean * inv0 + xsum * invr) / precision
  let sd = 1.0 / sqrt(precision)
  return [mean, sd, wsum]
}

pattern bandit_pick(seed: Float) -> Struct {
  let arms = query("SELECT id, name, prior_mean, prior_std FROM arm WHERE active = 1 ORDER BY id", [])
  let k = len(arms)
  if k == 0.0 {
    return {arm_id: 0.0, mode: "empty", theta: 0.0}
  }
  let rows = query("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM trial WHERE arm_id IS NOT NULL", [])
  let n = rows[0].n
  if to_int(n / explore_every) * explore_every == n {
    let step = to_int(n / explore_every)
    let kk = to_int(k)
    let idx = step - kk * to_int(step / kk)
    let arm = arms[idx]
    return {arm_id: arm.id, mode: "explore", theta: 0.0}
  }
  random_seed(seed)
  let mut i = 0.0
  let mut best_id = 0.0
  let mut best_theta = 0.0
  let mut first = true
  while i < k {
    let arm = arms[i]
    let post = arm_posterior(arm.id, arm.prior_mean, arm.prior_std)
    let theta = post[0] + post[1] * normal_sample(0.0, 1.0)
    if first == true {
      best_id = arm.id
      best_theta = theta
      first = false
    }
    if theta > best_theta {
      best_id = arm.id
      best_theta = theta
    }
    i = i + 1.0
  }
  return {arm_id: best_id, mode: "thompson", theta: best_theta}
}

pattern bandit_propose(trial_date: String, seed: Float) -> Float {
  let pick = bandit_pick(seed)
  if pick.arm_id == 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  let arm = query("SELECT id, day_window FROM arm WHERE id = ?", [pick.arm_id])
  if len(arm) == 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  let row = {trial_date: trial_date, day_window: arm[0].day_window, arm_id: pick.arm_id}
  return db_insert("trial", row)
}
// ── APP-MIRROR-END: bandit-core
// ── APP-MIRROR-START: telegram-core (byte-identical to
//    src/telegram/telegram.mlog §telegram-core) ────────────────────────

// Local wall-clock date of a unix timestamp, "YYYY-MM-DD" — the trial
// date is the OWNER's date, not UTC's (the 02:00 close already lives
// in the next local day). date_parts is chrono::Local-based
// (probe-pinned); the assembly is manual zero-padded.
pattern local_iso_date(unix_ts: Float) -> String {
  let p = date_parts(unix_ts)
  let mut mo = to_string(p.month)
  if p.month < 10.0 {
    mo = "0" + mo
  }
  let mut dd = to_string(p.day)
  if p.day < 10.0 {
    dd = "0" + dd
  }
  return to_string(p.year) + "-" + mo + "-" + dd
}

// Fold local wall-clock minutes to the UTC cron expression for a fixed
// local time. local_minutes = hour*60+minute in the OWNER's wall
// clock, tz_offset_hours = local = UTC + offset. No modulo operator:
// the +2880 pad keeps the subtraction non-negative before the
// truncating division (the bandit explore-idx precedent).
pattern cron_expr_for(local_minutes: Float, tz_offset_hours: Float) -> String {
  let off_min = to_int(tz_offset_hours * 60.0)
  let shifted = local_minutes - to_float(off_min) + 2880.0
  let day = to_int(shifted / 1440.0)
  let modm = shifted - day * 1440.0
  let hh = to_int(modm / 60.0)
  let mm = modm - hh * 60.0
  return to_string(mm) + " " + to_string(hh) + " * * *"
}

// Parse one chat text into the protocol answer. Returns
// {kind: "prediction"|"moment"|"note", value: Float, text: String}.
// to_float fails LOUD on garbage (the m0_row precedent) — a malformed
// p:/m: answer degrades to a note, never to a silent zero.
pattern parse_chat_text(raw_text: String) -> Struct {
  let text = trim(raw_text)
  if starts_with(text, "p:") {
    let rest = trim(substring(text, 2, len(text)))
    // №514: to_float fails LOUD on garbage — a malformed answer
    // degrades to a note through the explicit -1 sentinel, never to a
    // silent zero (a silent zero would fabricate a prediction).
    let v = to_float_or(rest, 0 - 1.0)
    if v < 0.0 {
      return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
    }
    return {kind: "prediction", value: v, text: text}
  }
  if starts_with(text, "m:") {
    let rest = trim(substring(text, 2, len(text)))
    let v = to_float_or(rest, 0 - 1.0)
    if v < 0.0 {
      return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
    }
    return {kind: "moment", value: v, text: text}
  }
  return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
}

// The morning proposal message. Every dynamic fragment passes
// escape_html — the acceptance row: DB output never reaches the chat
// raw.
pattern format_proposal(arm_name: String, note_body: String) -> String {
  return "Проба дня: " + escape_html(arm_name) + ". Нота: " + escape_html(note_body) + ". Ответь предсказанием: p:0..1"
}

// The evening report message.
pattern format_report(processed: Float, closed: Float, predictions: Float, moments: Float) -> String {
  return "Отчёт: обработано " + escape_html(to_string(processed)) + ", закрыто пропуском " + escape_html(to_string(closed)) + ", предсказаний " + escape_html(to_string(predictions)) + ", откликов " + escape_html(to_string(moments))
}

// The getUpdates URL with the offset + the long-poll timeout. The
// token lives in the URL path (the Bot API contract); it is read from
// the environment at the call site and never printed or echoed.
pattern get_updates_url(token: String, offset: Float) -> String {
  return "https://api.telegram.org/bot" + token + "/getUpdates?offset=" + to_string(offset) + "&timeout=25"
}

// One long-poll getUpdates with the №592 per-call deadline and the
// three-attempt caller-side retry (the language hides no retry inside,
// CHANGELOG-282). Returns the parsed update LIST — UNTRUSTED network
// data; the consumer must run it through the annotated boundary
// (process_updates). Empty List on exhausted retry: the caller
// distinguishes the drain outcome by the offset, silence is never
// fabricated as data.
pattern fetch_updates(token: String, offset: Float) -> List {
  let url = get_updates_url(token, offset)
  let mut attempt = 0.0
  while attempt < 3.0 {
    attempt = attempt + 1.0
    let r = try http_get(url, 40.0)
    // Sanitize-then-decide: escape_html restores integrity trust
    // (Sanitized = public/trusted); the raw label never branches.
    if escape_html(to_string(r.ok)) == "true" {
      return json_get(r.value, "result", [])
    }
    if attempt < 3.0 {
      sleep(15.0)
    }
  }
  return []
}
// ── APP-MIRROR-END: telegram-core
// ── The two cron ticks (the naryad: "два cron-тика в одном .mlog") ────

// The morning tick: propose an arm through the bandit core, write the
// trial (status 'proposed', the prediction fields stay at their
// defaults until the owner answers), message the owner. The proposal
// IS the prediction request — the owner answers p: during the day.
pattern tg_morning_tick() -> Unit {
  // Idempotent schema first: the tables exist even before the token
  // guard fires (the loud refusal must not leave an empty database).
  ensure_schema()
  // No early-return under a nested if (the D2-family case 4): the
  // guard inverts into a positive branch that carries the whole tick.
  let token = env_or("KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN", "")
  let chat_id = env_or("KAMERTON_CHAT_ID", "")
  if token != "" and chat_id != "" {
    let today = local_iso_date(now_unix())
    let tid = bandit_propose(today, now_unix())
    let mut msg = "Библиотека пуста — предложение не сформировано (громкий ноль бандита)"
    if tid != 0.0 {
      let arm_rows = query("SELECT a.name, n.body FROM trial t JOIN arm a ON a.id = t.arm_id LEFT JOIN note n ON n.id = t.note_id WHERE t.id = ?", [tid])
      if len(arm_rows) > 0.0 {
        msg = format_proposal(arm_rows[0].name, arm_rows[0].body)
      } else {
        msg = "Проба дня (trial #" + to_string(tid) + ")"
      }
    }
    let _ = send_message(chat_id, msg)
    print("[telegram] morning tick proposed trial " + to_string(tid))
  }
  if token == "" or chat_id == "" {
    print("[telegram] KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN/KAMERTON_CHAT_ID not set — morning tick refuses loudly")
  }
}

// The evening tick: drain getUpdates through the boundary, close the
// unanswered as misses (inside process_updates), report. Runs at 02:00
// LOCAL — the acceptance window closes without manual intervention.
pattern tg_evening_tick() -> Unit {
  ensure_schema()
  let token = env_or("KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN", "")
  let chat_id = env_or("KAMERTON_CHAT_ID", "")
  if token != "" and chat_id != "" {
    let today = local_iso_date(now_unix())
    let offset = to_float(kv_get("tg_offset"))
    let updates = fetch_updates(token, offset)
    process_updates(updates, chat_id, today, offset)
  }
  if token == "" or chat_id == "" {
    print("[telegram] KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN/KAMERTON_CHAT_ID not set — evening tick refuses loudly")
  }
}

// ── The idempotent registration + the serve surface ───────────────────


// Register the two ticks from the allowlisted offset. Idempotent across
// restarts AND repeated calls, AND a TZ-offset change: stale jobs (same
// prompt, a different expr — e.g. after KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET moved) are
// removed loudly, the current pair is added when missing.

mlogserver {
  port: 8461
  middleware: [rate_limit, security_headers]
  route "/health" method=GET {
    return respond("200 ok")
  }
  // Register the two cron ticks; call once after deploy (curl
  // http://127.0.0.1:8461/setup) — repeated calls and restarts are safe.
  route "/setup" method=GET {
    ensure_schema()
    setup_register()
    return respond("200 jobs=" + to_string(len(cron_list())))
  }
  route "/jobs" method=GET {
    let jobs = cron_list()
    let mut lines = ""
    each j in jobs {
      lines = lines + escape_html(j.cron_expr) + " -> " + escape_html(j.prompt) + "\n"
    }
    return respond("200 " + lines)
  }
  // Manual fire for the end-to-end check on a test chat (acceptance).
  route "/fire" method=GET {
    let jobs = cron_list()
    each j in jobs {
      let _ = cron_run(j.id)
    }
    return respond("200 fired")
  }
}

// ── Tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The suite is network-free: send_message degrades to the [AUDIT] stub
// without TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN (probe-pinned), fetch_updates is exercised
// against a refused endpoint through its retry/backoff shape, the DB
// effects run on the in-memory store.








